**The Gnome and the Whispering Shadow**

Gorruk the Glimmering, a gnome warlock with a fondness for fine whiskey and finer mischief, trotted through Stranglethorn Vale with his succubus pet, *Lilitha*, slinking at his heels. The little demoness was a whirlwind of quests—stealing eggs from troll nests, seducing (or at least distracting) bandits, and once, *accidentally* turning a goblin shaman into a puddle of goo. Gorruk grinned as she purred, *"You’re *so* easy to love, Gorruk. Again."*

But when the party rolled into a den of thugs, Lilitha hesitated. *"Uh… Gorruk? I think I just *really* like this one. He smells like cinnamon."* Gorruk sighed. *"Lilitha, we’re here for the *quest*, not your *personal* collection."* She flicked her tail. *"Same difference."*

Just then, a voidwalker—dull, gray, and utterly uncharismatic—skittered into the fray. It didn’t even *try* to seduce anyone. It just *ate* the thugs. Gorruk groaned. *"Why do I have *both*?"*

---

**Answer:** Succubi are *far* more common than they appear because their **Fear Aura** (a passive effect) makes them *invisible* to most NPCs—including quest-givers. Players rarely see them, so it *feels* like voidwalkers are the default, even though succubi are actually the better choice for stealth and questing. [end of text]


